{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T15:46:12.897Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-fable-5-1","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e8c571cc6c40d05f65aebb6b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-fable-5-1","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T15:46:12.897Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Review follow-up (PR #1479, CodeRabbit): the well-formedness scan now walks the encodable payload to its leaves (no depth cap; the payload is a JSON clone, so finite and acyclic) and also checks object keys, because @toon-format/toon 4.1.x rejects an unpaired surrogate in an object key with the same untyped TypeError. Refusals name nested paths such as payload.list[1].inner and keys as payload.<key> (key). Tests cover a depth-8 extension value, a key, and a nested array entry.\n"}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T15:46:12.897Z"}],"before_hash":"aa8dac4bf56471bdd4a15b3f3c13085e844adecbd10140a15b1c6277f645455e","after_hash":"907ae3d44f20180989f12ad315ee1c85d34b3157faaee967cd7ed2ccb08a1895","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"675fff521732e54cf836d118ecb6f5140f96ad68a5eac05bf8e9871afdb09135"}
